messages:
sophie_support: FYI escalation from Acme product team — they get a 400 from POST /v1/rerank. They say it worked yesterday and now fails. Server error: "items must be a non-empty array". Attaching payload they sent and response body.

sophie_support: ```json
{
  "request_id": "req_7b2a9",
  "items": {
    "id": "user-123",
    "candidates": "[]"
  }
}
```

sophie_support: response: ```json
{
  "error": {
    "type": "invalid_request",
    "message": "items must be a non-empty array",
    "code": 400
  }
}
```

jamal_ops: @sophie_support can you confirm Content-Type and full curl they used? also which SDK/version? :eyes:

sophie_support: They used our JS SDK via internal proxy. Content-Type: application/json. SDK reported v2.3.4 in the stack trace. Quick repro from their team: they call `api.rerank({ items: request.items })` where request.items comes from form-parsing middleware.

alex_devex: that payload looks like the middleware coerced arrays into strings or wrapped the object. "candidates": "[]" is the smoking gun — stringified array. JS SDK v2.3.4 had a bug where nested arrays from some parsers were serialized as strings on POST. We saw an incident last quarter.

maria_g: Can we get the raw network request from them (HAR) or a curl? If they can reproduce with curl we can rule out proxy.

sophie_support: they sent a curl repro: ```bash
curl -X POST https://api.redwood.ai/v1/rerank \ \
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer sk_live_xxx' \ \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \ \
  -d '{"request_id":"req_7b2a9","items":{"id":"user-123","candidates":"[]"}}'
```

jamal_ops: thanks. I repro locally by sending the same. Server rejects because `items` is not an array. Two actionable paths: 1) short-term: ask customer to change payload to "items": [{...}] and send candidates as arrays (workaround). 2) longer-term: track SDK fix and patch proxy.

alex_devex: I can confirm: patch for JS SDK v2.3.5 includes a serializer guard that ensures arrays remain arrays and rejects stringified arrays. I'll open a PR and coordinate a patch note. For now we should document the exact validation error in the support KB.

ci-bot: [integration-test] rerank-schema-tests failed on master at step validate-request -> error: items present but not array (test-case: wrapped_items_stringified_candidates).

maria_g: Can we provide the customer a small snippet they can drop into their code to fix? 

alex_devex: sure. Short snippet for Node/express to coerce: ```js
if (req.body && req.body.items && !Array.isArray(req.body.items)) {
  // sometimes body-parsers wrap a single item as object or string; normalize
  req.body.items = Array.isArray(req.body.items.items) ? req.body.items.items : [req.body.items];
}
if (req.body.items) {
  req.body.items = req.body.items.map(it => {
    if (typeof it.candidates === 'string') {
      try { it.candidates = JSON.parse(it.candidates); } catch(e) { /* leave as-is */ }
    }
    return it;
  });
}
```

sophie_support: passing that to the customer now. I've asked for HAR and proxy logs. Also asked them to try curl with the corrected `items` array.

jamal_ops: I'll file an incident-style internal note linking this thread and tag eng-runtime for follow-up on the SDK serialization fix. If customer still sees 400 after normalizing, escalate with HAR + full request_id.

alex_devex: PR opened for v2.3.5, adding extra tests. ETA to publish patch: ~2 hours. I'll post back once released.

sophie_support: Customer confirmed curl with corrected body succeeds. They applied the temporary fix. Marking issue as resolved on customer side. Leaving thread open until SDK patch is published. :white_check_mark:
